Title: gaze_close reads a real panel as seats: self-only when run from another project's cwd
Created: 2026-10-29
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-29T20:56Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
Reported by the DOIfetch session (raid f9e483, 2026-10-29) through the inter-project protocol; causes as its team lead stated them, not re-verified here.
`gaze_close.py` resolves the project from its cwd. Run from the harness directory, it read a real
panel as `seats: self-only` (DOIfetch PR #26, likely #19), which counts as no record
(`skills/merge/SKILL.md` § Gating tiers) and fired the gaze-self-only-twice breaker. This blocks merges.
Same family as the containment branch mismatch seen in harness PRs #1984 and #1996 today (the
runtime moved the gaze session's cwd during the run).

## Scope
Make gaze's close resolve the project and panel from explicit arguments or the review's own
record, never from the cwd at close time.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A test runs the close from a foreign cwd and records the real panel's seats
- [ ] The containment check reports the review tree, not the session's moved cwd
